    nq_carta_title: "Astral chart",
    nq_carta_desc: "Yours, someone else's, or that of an already-registered event (earthquakes, hurricanes...)",
    nq_eras_title: "Precessional ages",
    nq_eras_desc: "IAU/Newcomb and Dr. Raynaud de la Ferrière, compared, with live stars and sky cultures",
    mc_h2: "Cosmic Map",
    mc_p_intro: "Here's how the map below is organized — same layout, with what each part does. Rotate with the mouse, zoom with the wheel.",
    mc_diagrama_rota: "🖱️ rotate · 🔍 zoom<br><span style=\"opacity:.7\">(the detail of the chosen view appears below the map)</span>",
    mc_diagrama_elige: "↑<br><b>Choose view</b>",
    mc_diagrama_rota_zoom: "↑ <b>rotate / zoom here</b>",
    mc_diagrama_opciones: "↑<br><b>More options</b>",
    mc_p_iconos: "Each icon is a <b>category</b>, not a direct action: a click opens a small menu beside it with its options (🌌 = Solar System/Stars/Galaxy, same map at different zoom; 🗺️ = borders/names/highlight/measure; 🌐 = the 5 sky cultures). The ⛶ (fullscreen) is the only one that acts directly.",
    mc_p_barra_tiempo: "↑ <b>The time bar</b> — changes depending on the view chosen on the left; each one advances in a different time unit (see cards below). If it doesn't seem to match what you see, switch views and come back.",
    mc_p_que_mueve: "<b>🕰️ What each time bar moves, depending on the view:</b>",
    mc_tierra_title: "Earth: its movements",
    mc_tierra_desc: "0 to 1,000 days — with checkboxes to isolate rotation (real 24h), revolution (real 1 year), nutation and precession (sped up: real ≈18.6 and ≈25,772 years).",
    mc_sistema_title: "Solar System / Stars / Galaxy",
    mc_sistema_desc: "Real calendar years, from 1900 to 2100.",
    mc_carta_desc: "The exact date of the event you're viewing (years or days of a year, depending on the mode).",
    mc_topo_title: "Topocentrism (3D house sphere)",
    mc_topo_desc: "Minutes around the exact instant of the event (±12 hours).",
    nq_llona_title: "Llona's cycloid",
    mc_llona_desc: "Doesn't advance a real date: it plays back the full trace of the curve at the schematic speed you choose (0.1× to 2×).",
    mc_hint_riel: "<b>➡️ The rail on the right</b> is a set of quick shortcuts to extra controls, and it changes depending on the view chosen on the left. In \"Earth: its movements\": 🌍 = rotation/revolution/precession/nutation, 👁️ = camera views, ⏱️ = time scale. In Llona's cycloid, instead of those you get its own 3 controls directly: Case/Latitude φ/Rdr' curves. Almost no icon does anything when clicked directly — it opens a small floating menu right beside it with that group's options. The ⛶ (fullscreen) is the only one always there.",
    mc_rotate_hint: "🔄 Turn your phone to see it better",
