    mc_p_distancias: "Schematic distances, not to real scale — the goal is angular geometry (how aligned the planets are), not physical distance. Planetary positions: simplified Keplerian model for the browser (the platform uses Skyfield + JPL DE421 for real calculations).",
    mc_topo_dia_nota: "🕰️ When you move this control the <b>planets stay the same as in your chart</b> (their longitudes don't change) — the only thing that advances is the instant, and since the ASC is ALWAYS drawn fixed on the left, the whole wheel rearranges around it. That's why the planets seem to \"change\": really it's the frame of reference (the ASC) that rotates, not them.",
