    mc_eclipse_a: "A solar eclipse needs a New Moon (between Earth and Sun) exactly when the Moon crosses the ecliptic plane; a lunar one needs a Full Moon at that same crossing. Since the lunar orbit is tilted ≈5.14°, most months the Moon passes \"above or below\" the Earth-Sun line without aligning — it only coincides a couple of times a year (\"eclipse season\"). Here that coincidence is <b>forced</b> (the tilt is canceled for a moment) so the alignment is clear to see; on exit, the real tilt returns.",
    mc_llona_h: "🌀 Llona's cycloid — the real path of a crustal point",
    mc_llona_p1: "Combining rotation + revolution, a point on the crust does NOT trace a circle: it traces a cycloidal curve. Llona (TCC, Part XIV) argues that the <b>cusps</b> and <b>loops</b> of this curve mark points of dynamic tension in the crust.",
